# Rust
**/target/
corpus/generate/out/

# Python
**/__pycache__/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.venv/
**/dist/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
# The staged PyO3 extension for local dev/test — nested at hypertabular._native (the maturin
# module-name), built from the core crate's python feature. abi3 wheels carry one build per
# platform regardless of Python version (hence the plain and .abi3 spellings, not a
# per-version-tagged glob); .pyd covers Windows.
python/src/hypertabular/_native.so
python/src/hypertabular/_native.abi3.so
python/src/hypertabular/_native.pyd

# .NET
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
# CI (hyper-pack-nuget.yml) arranges and packs these per-RID at pack time; regenerable
# locally via `cargo cdylib` (the csproj's runtimes/**/native/* wildcard item).
csharp/HyperTabular/runtimes/
# The same for the static libraries a Native AOT publish links in: staged by the forge's
# static-libs/build-static-libs.sh at test and pack time, never committed.
csharp/HyperTabular/staticlibs/

# PHP
# Native libs under php/src/native/{rid}/ are not ignored: as in HyperCast, Packagist has no
# packing step — the git tree at the tag IS the package — so the libraries a release ships
# are committed there. Without one for the platform, the binding falls back to
# rust/target/release/ (`cargo cdylib`).
php/vendor/
php/composer.lock
php/.phpunit.result.cache
# The root composer.json exists only for Packagist, which reads the repository root; nothing
# here runs `composer install` from the root, and a stray local one should not be committed.
/vendor/
/composer.lock

# Swift
# The static libraries under swift/HyperTabularCore.artifactbundle/{triple}/ and
# swift/HyperTabularCoreApple.xcframework/, and the info.json and Info.plist that list them,
# are not ignored — as in HyperCast, where they are committed, because SwiftPM has no
# packing step for a git-URL dependency, and only by stage-native-binaries.yml, after their
# provenance checks. The forge's static-libs/build-static-libs.sh builds them too (CI runs
# it before every Swift step); a developer's own build of them shows up as modified or
# untracked and is not to be committed by hand.
**/.build/
# A library's pins are its consumers' to make: HyperCast is resolved fresh from the range
# the manifests declare, by CI as by anyone depending on this package.
/Package.resolved
/swift/Package.resolved
/swift/StaticSmokeTest/Package.resolved

# Gradle / Java
**/.gradle/
**/build/
# CI places each leg's native library here before `gradlew test`, and the Maven publish
# bundles every platform's at publish time; the local dev loop stages into
# build/generated-resources instead (already covered by **/build/ above), so anything here
# is regenerable via `cargo cdylib`.
java/src/main/resources/native/
# csharp/HyperTabular/build/ is NuGet's real, tracked build/{PackageId}.targets packaging
# convention, not a build output. It collides with **/build/ above, which would otherwise
# silently swallow anything new in it: the file would sit on disk, pack correctly in a
# local `dotnet pack`, and simply never exist in CI. Each directory level needs its own
# negation — git won't descend into an excluded directory to find a deeper !file
# re-inclusion — and gitignore rules apply in file order, so this must come after the rule
# it un-ignores. HyperCast carries the same block for the same reason.
!csharp/HyperTabular/build/
!csharp/HyperTabular/build/net11.0/
!csharp/HyperTabular/build/net11.0/HyperTabular.targets

# Ruby
# CI places each leg's native lib here for `bundle exec rspec` at build-native time, and the
# gem build stages every RID's into the gem; regenerable locally via `cargo cdylib`.
ruby/lib/hypertabular/native/*/
ruby/Gemfile.lock
ruby/pkg/
ruby/.yardoc/
# The wasm32-wasip1 archives `rake wasm:gem` packs (and their .gz), staged from CI's
# ruby-wasm-<minor> artifacts by release.yml, or by hand; never committed.
ruby/ext/hypertabular_native/*/
# rbwasm's interpreter build and its output, from running ruby/wasm-smoke locally.
ruby/wasm-smoke/Gemfile.lock
ruby/wasm-smoke/build/
ruby/wasm-smoke/rubies/
ruby/wasm-smoke/*.wasm
ruby/wasm-smoke/node_modules/
# The Magnus extension staged for local dev/test (`rake native:dev`, or CI's in-job copy),
# flat and per Ruby ABI (lib/hypertabular/<minor>/, which release.yml also writes from CI
# artifacts to pack the platform gems). Build output, never committed; scoped to the
# extension's filename so it cannot swallow a real lib/hypertabular/*.rb source file.
ruby/lib/hypertabular_native.so
ruby/lib/hypertabular_native.bundle
ruby/lib/hypertabular/*/hypertabular_native.so
ruby/lib/hypertabular/*/hypertabular_native.bundle

# go/staticlib's archives ARE committed — a Go module is whatever is in the tree — but only
# by the staging workflow, which adds them with `git add -f` after verifying each one's
# build provenance. Ignored here so that a developer's own build of them (the forge's
# static-libs/build-static-libs.sh, which `go test` needs to link) can never
# ride into a commit by accident.
go/staticlib/*/*.a

# BenchmarkDotNet
# Writes output relative to the process's working directory when invoked via `dotnet run`
# rather than the project directory, so this can land almost anywhere in the tree — not just
# csharp/HyperTabular.Benchmarks/. Criterion's own output already lands under rust/target/,
# covered by the **/target/ rule above.
**/BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# What Windows attaches to a downloaded file, when the file is copied into WSL.
*:Zone.Identifier

# The corpus copy test-apple-mobile stages for the Go suite in the iOS simulator
# (go_ios_exec carries only the module's testdata), if made by hand.
go/testdata/corpus/

# cargo-fuzz's working state: the corpora rust/fuzz/seed.py writes and libFuzzer grows, and
# the inputs it saves when a target fails. A failing input worth keeping becomes a test.
rust/fuzz/corpus/
rust/fuzz/artifacts/
rust/fuzz/coverage/
